/E (Developing Nations' Perspective: Developing economies \(led by nations like India and South Africa\) point out that as traditional physical goods digitize, border customs revenue from physical imports declines. They argue that restricting tariff mechanisms deprives developing states of traditional fiscal tools needed to generate sovereign revenue.)
