/Title (The institutional foundations of the World Trade Organization \(WTO\) lie in the post-World War II global effort to reconstruct international economic governance and prevent the severe economic protectionism that had exacerbated the Great Depression. At the Bretton Woods Conference in 1944, international leaders intended to create three pillars for global governance: the International Monetary Fund, the World Bank, and the International Trade Organization \(ITO\). Although fifty-three nations drafted the Havana Charter in 1948 to establish the ITO, the organization failed to materialize after the United States Congress refused to ratify the agreement, citing concerns over infringements on domestic economic sovereignty.)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1485 0 R
/Next 1506 0 R
>>
endobj
1498 0 obj
<<
/Title <494F4954204D554E903236>
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1485 0 R
/Prev 1507 0 R
>>
endobj
1499 0 obj
<<
/Title (First, the WTO is mandated to administer, implement, and monitor the covered multilateral trade agreements that form the legal foundation of global commerce. In executing this responsibility, the WTO enforces core statutory principles, most notably Most-Favoured-Nation \(MFN\) treatment, which strictly prohibits discrimination between foreign trading partners, and National Treatment, which requires imported products and services to receive non-discriminatory legal standing compared to domestic equivalents once they enter a domestic market.)
/Dest [19 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1469 0 R
/Prev 1486 0 R
/Next 1508 0 R
>>
endobj
1500 0 obj
<<
/Title (Fourth, the WTO maintains a systemic monitoring mandate through its Trade Policy Review Mechanism \(TPRM\), which conducts regular, transparent evaluations of individual member states' domestic economic regulations, state subsidies, and tariff frameworks. This surveillance capability increases market transparency, identifies protectionist measures early, and strengthens supply chain predictability for private commercial enterprises worldwide.)
/Dest [19 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1469 0 R
/Prev 1509 0 R
/Next 1487 0 R
>>
endobj
